Setup-phase sequence (AC.DSA.3 / D-DSA.4):

  1. Write the active-scope sentinel binding (component, ac_id)
     pairs from `new_acs` (A1's `write_active_scope_sentinel`
     API; consumer-only — no edits to A1 surface).
  2. Wait until the wall-clock advances to the next ISO second
     (Q1 empirical answer: A1's sentinel uses second-resolution
     `Z`-suffixed timestamps; A1's manifest uses microsecond-
     resolution `+00:00`-suffixed timestamps; lexicographic
     comparison collides on same-second writes because `.` (0x2E)
     < `Z` (0x5A); 100% collision rate without the wait).
  3. Register one manifest row per `NewACSpec` triple via A1's
     `register_source_binding` API (consumer-only).
  4. Author one placeholder test stub per `NewACSpec` at
     `framework/<comp>/tests/test_AC_<NORM>_placeholder.py` with
     a `pytest.skip(...)` body. Idempotent on byte-equal content;
     respects existing agent-authored content (D-DSA.5).

Behaviour:

  - DEV MODE + non-empty `new_acs`: setup phase fires; sentinel
    + manifest rows + stubs authored on disk; A2 + A3 admit the
    agent's first edit (composition test AC.DSA.8).
  - NORMAL USE: setup phase skipped entirely (AC.DSA.6).
    Mode-bit read only; sub-10ms.
  - Empty `new_acs` (research+plan dispatches; every amendment-#52
    caller): setup phase skipped (AC.DSA.1 / AC.DSA.10 backwards-
    compat).
  - Substrate failure (sentinel write fails, tracker raises, stub
    write fails): structured NDJSON diagnostic logged to
    `<workspace>/workspace/.pos/dispatch-wrapper.log`; dispatch
    proceeds (AC.DSA.5 fail-soft). A2/A3 surface the missing
    artefact at first-edit time.
  - Gate-chain refusal at activate_scope_with_spec: setup
    artefacts persist on disk (idempotent on retry per AC.DSA.4);
    operator observes refusal via diagnostic log + audit-trail of
    attempted setup.

Q1 empirical answer (sub-second collision rate, recorded per the
locked plan §6 D-DSA.4 caveat / halt-trigger 7):

  Without mitigation: 100% collision rate (1000/1000 in tight-
  loop empirical). The two A1 timestamp formats sort
  lexicographically wrong on same-second writes — `manifest >
  sentinel` evaluates False because the manifest's `.` byte sorts
  before the sentinel's `Z` byte. Resolution: deterministic wait
  until the wall clock advances to the next ISO second between
  sentinel write and the first manifest registration. With
  mitigation: 0% collision rate (100/100 verified). Worst-case
  wait <1s; typical <500ms. §14 method-decision register entry
  records this design choice.

ODD §2.5 reverse-direction audit clean: every code path, branch,
dependency, and test in the diff traces back to a named AC. No
silent exception branches; no defensive `if` for cases the ACs do
not name; no method-in-AC drift.

